{"w": 595.3200073242188, "h": 809.0257568359375, "lines": [{"t": "91", "x": 0.9080829955905043, "y": 0.9742087522985531, "w": 0.0256602530131315, "h": 0.017428414981790374, "c": 1, "size": 12.0, "bold": false}, {"t": "READING PASSAGE 2", "x": 0.10727675473252624, "y": 0.15349074143509378, "w": 0.29072257844517424, "h": 0.023179739115831682, "c": 1, "size": 16.0, "bold": true}, {"t": "Can the planet's coral reefs be saved?", "x": 0.24373446939184146, "y": 0.2165073264751818, "w": 0.5552441872708503, "h": 0.026142565890596797, "c": 1, "size": 18.0, "bold": true}, {"t": "A", "x": 0.10727675473252624, "y": 0.2549090431606664, "w": 0.02084419457062703, "h": 0.01882263537038409, "c": 1, "size": 13.0, "bold": true}, {"t": "14", "x": 0.12582140429864574, "y": 0.28579803528881537, "w": 0.027866154287957533, "h": 0.01882263537038409, "c": 1, "size": 13.0, "bold": false}, {"t": "Conservationists have put the final touches to a giant artificial reef they have been", "x": 0.10727675473252624, "y": 0.3356357465418159, "w": 0.8261206772019258, "h": 0.01882263537038409, "c": 1, "size": 13.0, "bold": false}, {"t": "assembling at the world-renowned Zoological Society of London (London Zoo).", "x": 0.10727675473252624, "y": 0.3559564870157686, "w": 0.8032743240709215, "h": 0.01882263537038409, "c": 1, "size": 13.0, "bold": false}, {"t": "Samples of the planet's most spectacular corals - vivid green branching coral,", "x": 0.10727675473252624, "y": 0.3862150792322761, "w": 0.8266050050836998, "h": 0.01882263537038409, "c": 1, "size": 13.0, "bold": false}, {"t": "yellow scroll, blue ridge and many more species - have been added to the giant", "x": 0.10727675473252624, "y": 0.4065358574276213, "w": 0.8265913692648438, "h": 0.01882263537038409, "c": 1, "size": 13.0, "bold": false}, {"t": "tank along with fish that thrive in their presence: blue tang, clownfish and many", "x": 0.10727675473252624, "y": 0.4270049184169267, "w": 0.826629611072613, "h": 0.01882263537038409, "c": 1, "size": 13.0, "bold": false}, {"t": "others. The reef is in the zoo's new gallery, Tiny Giants, which is dedicated to the", "x": 0.10727675473252624, "y": 0.4473256588908794, "w": 0.8259900604107785, "h": 0.01882263537038409, "c": 1, "size": 13.0, "bold": false}, {"t": "minuscule invertebrate creatures that sustain life across the planet. The coral reef", "x": 0.10727675473252624, "y": 0.4678194273922794, "w": 0.8262950721483479, "h": 0.01882263537038409, "c": 1, "size": 13.0, "bold": false}, {"t": "tank and its seven-metre-wide window form the core of the exhibition.", "x": 0.10727675473252624, "y": 0.4881401678662321, "w": 0.7149521008542071, "h": 0.01882263537038409, "c": 1, "size": 13.0, "bold": false}, {"t": "'Coral reefs are the most diverse ecosystems on Earth and we want to show", "x": 0.10727675473252624, "y": 0.5486573900206396, "w": 0.8259030167249982, "h": 0.01882263537038409, "c": 1, "size": 13.0, "bold": false}, {"t": "people how wonderful they are,' said Paul Pearce-Kelly, senior curator of", "x": 0.10727675473252624, "y": 0.5689781304945923, "w": 0.8265510769579985, "h": 0.01882263537038409, "c": 1, "size": 13.0, "bold": false}, {"t": "invertebrates and fish at the Zoological Society of London. 'However, we also", "x": 0.10727675473252624, "y": 0.5894471914838977, "w": 0.8260553688063522, "h": 0.01882263537038409, "c": 1, "size": 13.0, "bold": false}, {"t": "want to highlight the research and conservation efforts that are now being carried", "x": 0.10727675473252624, "y": 0.6097679319578504, "w": 0.8263835511834814, "h": 0.01882263537038409, "c": 1, "size": 13.0, "bold": false}, {"t": "out to try to save them from the threat of global warming.' They want people to", "x": 0.10727675473252624, "y": 0.6302369552257633, "w": 0.8261425150170862, "h": 0.018822673091776602, "c": 1, "size": 13.0, "bold": false}, {"t": "see what is being done to try to save these wonders.", "x": 0.10727675473252624, "y": 0.650557771142501, "w": 0.533889802898852, "h": 0.018822673091776602, "c": 1, "size": 13.0, "bold": false}, {"t": "B", "x": 0.10727675473252624, "y": 0.7111120734257467, "w": 0.019836335827867986, "h": 0.018822673091776602, "c": 1, "size": 13.0, "bold": true}, {"t": "15", "x": 0.12582140429864574, "y": 0.7419639477036649, "w": 0.028067718347137807, "h": 0.018822673091776602, "c": 1, "size": 13.0, "bold": false}, {"t": "Corals are composed of tiny animals, known as polyps, with tentacles for", "x": 0.10727675473252624, "y": 0.7918016778173618, "w": 0.8267303931022031, "h": 0.018822673091776602, "c": 1, "size": 13.0, "bold": false}, {"t": "capturing small marine creatures in the sea water. These polyps are transparent", "x": 0.10727675473252624, "y": 0.8121224182913145, "w": 0.8259901629357324, "h": 0.018822673091776602, "c": 1, "size": 13.0, "bold": false}, {"t": "but get their brilliant tones of pink, orange, blue, green, etc. from algae that live", "x": 0.10727675473252624, "y": 0.8324431587652672, "w": 0.8259244444403434, "h": 0.018822673091776602, "c": 1, "size": 13.0, "bold": false}, {"t": "within them, which in turn get protection, while their photosynthesising of the", "x": 0.10727675473252624, "y": 0.8529122197545725, "w": 0.8268583442445515, "h": 0.018822673091776602, "c": 1, "size": 13.0, "bold": false}, {"t": "sun's rays provides nutrients for the polyps. This comfortable symbiotic", "x": 0.10727675473252624, "y": 0.8732577054620124, "w": 0.8261424124921325, "h": 0.018822673091776602, "c": 1, "size": 13.0, "bold": false}, {"t": "relationship has led to the growth of coral reefs that cover 0.1% of the planet's", "x": 0.10727675473252624, "y": 0.8937267664513178, "w": 0.8259248545401586, "h": 0.018822673091776602, "c": 1, "size": 13.0, "bold": false}, {"t": "ocean bed while providing homes for more than 25% of marine species, including", "x": 0.10727675473252624, "y": 0.9140475069252705, "w": 0.8262295587028666, "h": 0.018822673091776602, "c": 1, "size": 13.0, "bold": false}, {"t": "fish, molluscs, sponges and shellfish.", "x": 0.10727675473252624, "y": 0.9343682473992232, "w": 0.3814675944764886, "h": 0.018822673091776602, "c": 1, "size": 13.0, "bold": false}], "source": "pdf text layer"}